To solve the given problem, we start by finding the value of $x$ modulo $20$ using the given congruences. We have:

\begin{align*}
4x &\equiv 8 \pmod{20}, \\
3x &\equiv 16 \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}

To find $x$, we subtract the second congruence from the first:

\begin{align*}
x &\equiv (4x - 3x) \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv (8 - 16) \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv -8 \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}

Since we are interested in the remainder when $x^2$ is divided by $20$, we square the value of $x$ modulo $20$:

\begin{align*}
x^2 &\equiv (-8)^2 \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv 64 \pmod{20} \\
&\equiv 4 \pmod{20}.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the remainder when $x^2$ is divided by $20$ is $\boxed{4}$.

