To factor the expression $x(x+2)+(x+2)$, we look for common factors in each term. We notice that $(x+2)$ is a common factor. Thus, we can rewrite the expression by factoring $(x+2)$ out:

\begin{align*}
x(x+2)+(x+2) &= (x+2) \cdot x + (x+2) \cdot 1 \\
&= (x+2)(x+1) \\
&= \boxed{(x+1)(x+2)}
\end{align*}

This step-by-step approach shows how we factor out the common term $(x+2)$ and rewrite the expression as the product of $(x+1)$ and $(x+2)$.

